Add duckdb_v2_result_take_collection: hand over a retained result's rows

A step of a retained C API v2 result copies its next chunk out of the column
data collection holding the rows, into a chunk allocated for the step
(ChunkRetainedCollection::FetchRaw, with DISALLOW_ZERO_COPY). A client that
must free the connection as soon as the query ends, and so steps every chunk
before reading any, holds the rows twice: the collection until the last step,
and the copies. It then copies them once more into its own format. The engine
can hand the collection over instead (QueryResult::TakeCollection), and v2
already scans a collection into a caller-owned chunk, zero-copy where possible.
Born from reading 20M rows of two columns into NumPy through v2: 631 MB held
after stepping, 320 MB once the collection is taken; 27 ms to convert 10M rows,
20 ms scanning the taken collection.

  - ResultWrapperV2::TakeCollection(): for a retained chunk result whose
    execution has ended, hands over the collection and finishes the result,
    releasing the connection. Null while the query still runs; an error for a
    result that streams, has handed out a chunk, or has ended.
  - duckdb_v2_result_take_collection(result, &collection), in
    duckdb_v2_result_take_collection.h.

Note for upstreaming: duckdb_v2.h is generated; an upstream PR would add this
to its generator's definitions.
